.TH WLCROSSHAIR 1 "2026-08-24" "wlcrosshair 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlcrosshair \- crosshair overlay for Wayland compositors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlcrosshair
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlcrosshair
is a minimal crosshair overlay for Wayland compositors that support the
wlr-layer-shell protocol (e.g.\& Hyprland, Sway, COSMIC, niri, KDE Plasma).
.PP
It runs as a background daemon, drawing a crosshair image on a layer-shell
surface at the overlay layer, above all other windows including fullscreen
applications and games.  It listens on a Unix socket for commands from
.BR wlcrosshairctl (1).
.PP
The crosshair starts hidden.  Use
.B wlcrosshairctl
to toggle, show, hide, or reload the overlay.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.I ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml
(respects
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
.SS Config Fields
.TP
.BI path " = " PATH
.I (required)
Path to a PNG crosshair image.  Tilde expansion is supported.
.TP
.BI output " = " NAME
.I (optional)
Wayland output name as reported by the compositor (e.g.\&
.BR DP-1 ,
.BR eDP-1 ,
.BR HDMI-A-1 ).
If omitted, the only connected output is used.  With several displays,
the name that sorts first alphabetically is used by default.
See
.B FINDING THE OUTPUT NAME
below.
.TP
.BI size " = " PIXELS
.I (optional)
Set both width and height to this value, overriding separate dimensions.
If omitted, each dimension
defaults to the PNG's actual dimension unless set separately below.
.TP
.BI width " = " PIXELS
.I (optional)
Width of the crosshair in pixels; defaults to the PNG's width if
.B size
is unset.
.TP
.BI height " = " PIXELS
.I (optional)
Height of the crosshair in pixels; defaults to the PNG's height if
.B size
is unset.
.TP
.BI opacity " = " VALUE
.I (optional; defaults to 1.0)
Opacity multiplier from 0.0 (invisible) to 1.0 (original image opacity).
The value multiplies the PNG image's existing alpha, so transparent pixels
remain transparent.
.SS Example Config
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
path = "~/.config/wlcrosshair/rotated.png"
.fi
.RE
.SH FINDING THE OUTPUT NAME
Set
.B output
to select a particular display.  Run the command for your compositor in
a terminal inside your Wayland session.  Look for names such as
.BR eDP-1 ,
.BR HDMI-A-1 ,
or
.BR DP-2 :
.TP
.B KDE Plasma
.B kscreen-doctor -o
.TP
.B Hyprland
.B hyprctl monitors
.TP
.B Sway
.B swaymsg -t get_outputs
.TP
.B COSMIC
.B cosmic-randr list
.TP
.B niri
.B niri msg outputs
.TP
.B Other wlroots-based compositors
.B wlr-randr
.TP
.B Other non-wlroots compositors
.B wayland-info
.PP
Use the output name, not a numeric ID or a monitor description.
.B wlr-randr
requires wlr-output-management support;
.B wayland-info
can show names when the compositor advertises
.BR zxdg_output_manager_v1 .
Matching a specified name also requires that protocol.  The compositor
must support
.B zwlr_layer_shell_v1
for this program to work; GNOME does not provide the required layer-shell
protocol.
.PP
Set the discovered name in
.IR ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml ,
for example:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
output = "eDP-1"
.fi
.RE
Output names can change when switching ports, docks or hardware; check
again if the overlay cannot find the configured output.
.SH SOCKET
.B wlcrosshair
listens on
.I /tmp/crosshair.sock
for IPC commands (one per line).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Override the config directory.  Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/wlcrosshair/config.toml
Default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wlcrosshairctl (1)
